"answer": "Project Zenith has received executive budget approval of $2M, though a later update indicates an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses. The project team was expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, ahead-of-schedule testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics. The project is moving through development phases, with upcoming activities including user interface enhancements in October, a staff meeting on November 20th to discuss the analytics report, and the implementation of updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year. Additionally, partnership discussions with TechInnovate for AI technology are in early stages."
